Title: FUN'S Cross-Word Puzzles
Author: Olga Lehander
Copyright: New York World
Date: 1914-04-26
Number: 19
Notes: A 13x13 stepped diamond with a cross-shaped blank in the centre (shown as _), printed "No 19" (the number is from the centre block). Credit in the intro: "It was sent in by Miss Olga Lehander of East Seventy-sixth street, New York City." Printed intro: "Here is a very cleverly constructed cross word puzzle for you to work out. It was sent in by Miss Olga Lehander of East Seventy-sixth street, New York City. Can you solve it? Fill in the small squares with letters spelling words corresponding to the list of clews and definitions given below. The solutions will be given in next week's FUN." Read by hand from the Milwaukee Sentinel's page (Milwaukee_Sentinel_1914_04_26_90.png), solution from Milwaukee_Sentinel_1914_05_03_97.png, by Claude, 2026-11-16.


