1-2. The side opposite to that from which the wind blows. ~ LEE
3-4. Sums of money that are lent. ~ LOANS
5-6. To reply. ~ RESPOND
7-8. It floats. ~ BOAT
9-10. Perceives. ~ SEES
11-12. What grass seed is. ~ SOWN
13-14. A reflected sound. ~ ECHO
15-16. Used by plumbers. ~ LEAD
17-18. A gentlewoman. ~ LADY
19-20. Where you can find a portion of Turkey. ~ ASIA
21-22. To wait for. ~ BIDE
23-24. A canvas shelter. ~ TENT
25-26. Mentally sound. ~ SANE
27-28. Dots. ~ STIPPLE
29-30. Rapidity of motion. ~ SPEED
25-32. The past tense of speed. ~ SPED
31-32. Turf. ~ SOD
33-34. Always look before you do this. ~ LEAP
35-36. A Mexican laborer. ~ PEON
1-8. Not sound. ~ LOST
3-12. To incline. ~ LEAN
5-27. Roughs. ~ ROWDIES
7-23. To brag. ~ BOAST
11-19. An ocean. ~ SEA
2-9. A son of Seth. ~ ENOS
4-13. A knife. ~ SNEE
6-28. To refuse. ~ DECLINE
10-26. A place sheltered from strong lignt. ~ SHADE
14-22. A lyric poem. ~ ODE
20-29. Insects. ~ ANTS
24-31. Appreciated by waiters. ~ TIPS
21-30. A hairless scalp. ~ BALD



